{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773076556,"nonce":"fIWg6yENLae2T6CsKK1+/98uhkc=","title":"Graph state not live-coupled: manual save only, tab label wrong, PWA serves stale","message":"Three related issues all stemming from loose coupling between UI state and persisted state.\n\n## 1. No auto-save — manual Cmd+S required\n`toggleNodeReversed`, node moves, collapses etc. all correctly set `isDirty: true` but nothing auto-saves. A refresh after any change without explicit save loses work. PWA caching makes this worse: first reload may serve stale cached version, second reload hits server.\n\n**Fix**: debounced auto-save (800ms after last dirty change). Same code path as Cmd+S.\n\n## 2. Tab label shows \"Model\" instead of project name\n`openProjectInTab` sets `currentGraphLabel: graph.metadata?.name ?? \"Model\"` where `graph` is the `GraphSpec`. `GraphSpec.metadata` is frequently `null`. The project-level name lives in `project.metadata.name` and is not threaded through.\n\n**Fix**: pass `project.metadata.name` as the tab label when opening a project.\n\n## 3. PWA cache serves stale API responses on hard refresh\nSafari PWA Cmd+Shift+R raises a plain-text overlay instead of doing a hard refresh. Service worker caches API responses, so first reload can serve stale graph data.\n\n**Fix**: set `Cache-Control: no-store` on all `/api/graphs/*` responses, and update service worker fetch handler to never cache API calls.\n\n## Attempt tracking\n(Add comments here for each fix attempt)","files":null}]}